  "content": {
    "id": "p30-stem-61-64",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $0\\leq x\\leq2\\pi$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q61",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\left(x-\\frac\\pi3\\right)=-\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
          "worked": "The modified domain is $-\\frac\\pi3\\leq x-\\frac\\pi3\\leq\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$. The related angle is $\\frac\\pi6$. Sine is negative in quadrants 3 and 4; subtracting $2\\pi$ where needed gives the two arguments in this domain.\n$$\\begin{align*}x-\\frac\\pi3&=-\\frac\\pi6,\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\\\x&=-\\frac\\pi6+\\frac\\pi3,\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{6}+\\frac\\pi3\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi6,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q62",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\left(x+\\frac\\pi4\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{19\\pi}{12},\\ \\frac{23\\pi}{12}$.",
          "worked": "The modified domain is $\\frac\\pi4\\leq x+\\frac\\pi4\\leq\\frac{9\\pi}{4}$. The related angle is $\\frac\\pi6$; cosine is positive in quadrants 1 and 4. The arguments in this domain are $\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$ and $\\frac{13\\pi}{6}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac\\pi4&=\\frac{11\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{13\\pi}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{11\\pi}{6}-\\frac\\pi4,\\ \\frac{13\\pi}{6}-\\frac\\pi4\\\\x&=\\frac{19\\pi}{12},\\ \\frac{23\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q63",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\left(x-\\frac\\pi3\\right)=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi{12},\\ \\frac{13\\pi}{12}$.",
          "worked": "The modified domain is $-\\frac\\pi3\\leq x-\\frac\\pi3\\leq\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$. The related angle is $\\frac\\pi4$. Tangent is negative in quadrants 2 and 4, with period $\\pi$; the arguments in this domain are $-\\frac\\pi4$ and $\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x-\\frac\\pi3&=-\\frac\\pi4,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\\\x&=-\\frac\\pi4+\\frac\\pi3,\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{4}+\\frac\\pi3\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi{12},\\ \\frac{13\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q64",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x-2\\pi}{3}\\right)=-\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac32,\\ \\frac{11}{2}$.\n\nTransform the complete argument domain before solving; these values of $x$ are exact.",
          "worked": "The modified domain is $-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\leq\\frac{\\pi x-2\\pi}{3}\\leq\\frac{2\\pi^2-2\\pi}{3}$. Its upper endpoint lies between $\\frac{7\\pi}{6}$ and $\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$. The related angle is $\\frac\\pi6$; extending the negative sine branches by $2\\pi$ leaves only $-\\frac\\pi6$ and $\\frac{7\\pi}{6}$ in this domain.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\pi x-2\\pi}{3}&=-\\frac\\pi6,\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\\\\\pi x-2\\pi&=-\\frac\\pi2,\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\\\\\pi x&=\\frac{3\\pi}{2},\\ \\frac{11\\pi}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac32,\\ \\frac{11}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy $0\\leq x\\leq2\\pi$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 74
      }
    ]
  },
